How you will make an impact?

We are seeking a Program and Portfolio Manager for our Digital Transformation Office (DTO) Team. In this role, you will act as a senior individual contributor driving the execution of our IT Strategy in line with our sCore direction. You will operate with strong focus on technical delivery, ensuring that complex digital initiatives are not only well-governed, but also technically sound and executable. By aligning strategy with execution, providing value transparency, and ensuring sound portfolio and strategic roadmap governance, you will be at the center of IT-enabled transformation!

Job Description

Your Responsibilities:

- Own and continuously refine a multi-year digital delivery roadmap, ensuring feasibility and sequencing across systems and platforms;
- Main task: Oversee and challenge complex, cross-platform initiatives with a strong focus on project management and technical integrity, dependencies, risk and in-time delivery;
- Act as Program Manager for selected key initiatives, with hands-on involvement in structuring, planning, and execution tracking;
- Ensure end-to-end transparency on delivery, including progress, risks, trade-offs, and value realization;
- Ensure business case validity, tracking and delivery of expected outcomes;
- Whenever needed – ensure rapid turnaround of strategic initiatives;
- Establish and drive governance structures to ensure successful delivery (including Steering Committees with executive stakeholders);
- Work closely with platform leads, architecture and engineering leads to validate solution approaches and delivery plans;
- Work closely with CIO Office incl. flexibility for ad-hoc work related to CIO priorities;
- Drive pragmatic change and adoption, ensuring initiatives land effectively in the organization.

Qualifications

Required key competencies and qualifications:

- 7+ years of experience either in enterprise IT or top-tier IT consultancy;
- Proven track record of managing complex, large-scale digital programs and portfolios;
- Strong hands-on understanding of IT build and delivery (e.g. product delivery, engineering, integration, infrastructure & services, legacy modernization etc.);
- Ability to bring structure and clarity to ambiguous topics and turn them into actionable plans;
- Comfortable working hands-on and independently, without formal team leadership;
- Strong senior stakeholder management and reporting skills, with the ability to challenge constructively;
- Very good fluency in English (written and verbal), German preferred.

